WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.400
That old

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.120
help page

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:01.520
is no

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:02.400
longer useful.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.040
You delete

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:03.360
it from

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.080
your folder.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.120
But that deletion

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:05.600
still needs

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:05.840
to be

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:06.400
prepared for

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:06.720
the next

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.360
commit.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:07.920
The folder

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:08.240
and the

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.360
next snapshot are

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.360
different views.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:13.160
For a

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:13.960
tracked file,

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.880
Git’s removal command normally

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:16.440
removes the

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.560
working copy and

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:18.200
its entry

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:18.440
in the

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.560
staging area,

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.200
also called

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.240
the index.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:21.640
The next

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.760
commit is prepared

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:23.240
to leave

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.240
that page out.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:26.400
Another form keeps

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:26.960
the local

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.160
file while removing

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:28.800
its entry

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:29.040
from the

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:29.760
index.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.320
A file

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:30.800
can stay

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:31.120
in your

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:31.840
folder without

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:32.480
being included

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:32.640
in the

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.480
next commit.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:35.640
Neither form makes

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.040
a commit

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:36.600
for you.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.200
Earlier commits still contain

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:38.600
the page

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:39.480
they recorded.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.120
Removing a

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:40.680
file now

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:41.080
does not

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:42.280
erase its history.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:42.880
Think.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.200
Prepare its absence,

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.200
then commit.

